.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bristlenose
processes user-research interview recordings into structured, themed, timestamped
quotes. It transcribes audio on your machine using Whisper, then extracts and
enriches quotes via an LLM \(em Claude, ChatGPT, Azure OpenAI or Gemini in the
cloud, or a local model via Ollama \(em groups them by screen and theme, and
renders a browsable HTML report you own as a file.
.PP
The transcription pass runs locally. The analysis pass sends transcript text to
the provider you choose; with a cloud provider that text leaves your machine.
Use \fB\-\-redact\-pii\fR to strip personal data before the analysis pass, or
\fB\-\-llm local\fR to keep the whole pipeline on your own hardware.
.PP
The HTML report includes sections (grouped by screen), themes (cross-participant
patterns), a sentiment histogram, friction points, user journeys, clickable
timecodes with a popout video player, starred quotes with CSV export, inline
editing, and a tag system with auto-suggest.
.PP
.B First-run preflight.
On every \fBrun\fR / \fBtranscribe\fR / \fBanalyze\fR invocation \fBbristlenose\fR
runs a short block of preflight checks after the input scan but before any
stage executes. Each check fires only when needed:
.IP \(bu 4
\fBWhisper model\fR \(em if the model isn't fully cached, prints a framed banner
(model name, \(ti1.5 GB, Ctrl+C-resumable) and lets Hugging Face Hub print its
own progress natively. Use \fB\-\-no\-fetch\fR to abort instead, or run
\fBbristlenose doctor \-\-fetch\fR up front.
.IP \(bu 4
\fBffmpeg\fR \(em if not on PATH, prints a per-distro install table. On
macOS with Homebrew installed and its prefix writable, offers to run
\fBbrew install ffmpeg\fR (default: \fBn\fR; an explicit \fBy\fR is required
before any system mutation).
.IP \(bu 4
\fBAPI-key validation\fR \(em for Anthropic / OpenAI providers, runs a paid
single-token \fI/messages\fR call (\(ti$0.0001) to verify the key works and
has billing balance, before any transcription begins. Result cached for
24 hours per provider in the state file (see \fBFILES\fR). Set
\fBBRISTLENOSE_SKIP_PREFLIGHT=1\fR to skip.
.IP \(bu 4
\fBspaCy PII model\fR \(em fetched lazily on the first
\fB\-\-redact\-pii\fR run; one inline line, no banner.
.PP
The block ends with a closing line (\fINo more questions. \(ti<X> min to your
report. Ctrl+C anytime.\fR) after which no prompt fires for the rest of the run.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B run
Full pipeline: ingest files, transcribe, identify speakers, extract quotes,
cluster by screen, group by theme, update participant registry, render HTML and
Markdown reports. Requires an API key. PII redaction is off by default; use
\fB\-\-redact\-pii\fR to enable.
.TP
.B transcribe
Transcription only. No LLM calls, no API key needed. Produces raw transcript
files in \fIbristlenose-output/transcripts-raw/\fR.
.TP
.B analyze
Run LLM analysis on existing transcript \fI.txt\fR files. Skips ingestion and
transcription. Useful after reviewing or editing raw transcripts.
.TP
.B analyse
British English alias for \fBanalyze\fR.
.TP
.B serve \fR[\fIproject-dir\fR]
Open a previous report in your browser (no analysis). Launches a local web
server and opens the React interface. Auto-renders intermediate data before
serving so the report always matches the current code. The \fB[serve]\fR extras
are installed by default with the standard distributions (brew, pip with
extras, snap) and are checked by \fBbristlenose doctor\fR.
.IP
With the optional \fB[mcp]\fR extra installed
(\fBpip install 'bristlenose[mcp]'\fR), serve also mounts a read-only Model
Context Protocol endpoint at \fB/mcp/\fR, and prints the address and bearer
token an agent needs. It offers four tools over the curated report \(em project
overview, quote search, signals, and codebook \(em so an MCP client (Claude
Code, Claude Desktop, ChatGPT, Codex) can answer questions about the study.
Read-only: no writes, no filesystem paths, and no LLM calls from Bristlenose.
Participant names accompany speaker codes unless the project's anonymise
setting is on. Leave the server running while the agent is connected.
.TP
.B status \fIproject-dir\fR
Show pipeline status for a project. Reads the manifest and prints which stages
are complete, partial, or pending, with session counts and intermediate file
validation. Accepts either the input directory or the output directory.
No LLM calls, no network — purely offline. Use \fB\-v\fR for per-session detail.
.TP
.B doctor
Check runtime dependencies and show tailored fix instructions. Tests FFmpeg,
transcription backend, Whisper model cache, API key validity, network
connectivity, PII redaction dependencies, and disk space. Also runs automatically
on first invocation and as a pre-flight check before pipeline commands.
.TP
.B configure \fIprovider\fR [\fB\-k\fR \fIKEY\fR]
Store API credentials securely in the system credential store (macOS Keychain
or Linux Secret Service). Provider can be \fBclaude\fR (or \fBanthropic\fR),
\fBchatgpt\fR (or \fBopenai\fR, \fBgpt\fR), \fBazure\fR (or
\fBazure-openai\fR), \fBgemini\fR (or \fBgoogle\fR), \fBlocal\fR (or
\fBollama\fR), or \fBmiro\fR.
The key is validated with a test API call before storing (Azure validates
via \fBbristlenose doctor\fR instead, since it also needs endpoint and
deployment). Where no keyring is available \(em a headless server, for
instance \(em the key is persisted to a permission-protected config file
instead, so the command always leaves you configured. Use \fB\-k\fR to provide
the key non-interactively.
Storing a key also makes that provider current for analysis \(em announced in
the output, and reversible any time with \fBbristlenose use\fR.
.TP
.B use \fIprovider\fR
Choose which AI provider runs the analysis: \fBclaude\fR, \fBchatgpt\fR,
\fBgemini\fR, \fBazure\fR, or \fBlocal\fR. The choice persists in your
user-level config until you change it \(em keys stay stored, so switching
never means re-entering one. \fB\-\-llm\fR and \fBBRISTLENOSE_LLM_PROVIDER\fR
still override it per run.
.TP
.B codebooks
List the codebook frameworks available to AutoCode, with the slug to pass to
\fB\-\-codebook\fR.
.TP
.B pipeline
Show which models Bristlenose currently uses at each pipeline stage \(em
transcription backend, the chosen LLM provider and model per analysis stage,
and the anonymisation engine \(em followed by a host context strip. Read-only:
to change a backend, edit your settings or \fI.env\fR. The Settings \(-> Pipeline
tab in the report UI shows the same information.
.TP
.B help \fR[\fItopic\fR]
Show detailed help. Topics: \fBcommands\fR, \fBconfig\fR, \fBworkflows\fR, or
any command name.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Global options
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-lang " " \fICODE\fR
Interface language. One of \fBen\fR, \fBes\fR, \fBca\fR, \fBja\fR, \fBfr\fR,
\fBde\fR, \fBko\fR, \fBcs\fR, \fBit\fR, \fBpl\fR, \fBru\fR, \fBuk\fR, \fBda\fR,
\fBsv\fR, \fBnb\fR, \fBtr\fR, \fBnl\fR, \fBfi\fR, \fBpt-BR\fR, \fBpt-PT\fR,
\fBzh-Hant\fR, \fBzh-Hant-HK\fR. Also settable via \fBBRISTLENOSE_LANG\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-install\-completion
Install shell completion for the current shell.
.TP
.BR \-\-show\-completion
Print shell completion for the current shell, to copy or customise.
.TP
.BR \-\-help
Show command help and exit.
.SS Options for \fBrun\fR
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " " \fIDIR\fR
Output directory. Default: \fIbristlenose-output/\fR inside the input folder.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-project " " \fINAME\fR
Project name for the report header. Defaults to the input folder name.
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-whisper\-backend " " \fIBACKEND\fR
Transcription backend: \fBauto\fR (detect hardware), \fBmlx\fR (Apple Silicon GPU),
\fBfaster-whisper\fR (CUDA/CPU). Default: \fBauto\fR.
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-whisper\-model " " \fIMODEL\fR
Whisper model size: \fBtiny\fR, \fBbase\fR, \fBsmall\fR, \fBmedium\fR,
\fBlarge-v3\fR, \fBlarge-v3-turbo\fR. Default: \fBlarge-v3-turbo\fR.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-llm " " \fIPROVIDER\fR
LLM provider: \fBclaude\fR (or \fBanthropic\fR), \fBchatgpt\fR (or \fBopenai\fR),
\fBazure\fR (or \fBazure-openai\fR), \fBgemini\fR (or \fBgoogle\fR),
\fBlocal\fR (or \fBollama\fR). If not given, the provider you last set with
\fBconfigure\fR or \fBuse\fR is used; with a single configured provider, that
one. With several keys and no choice recorded, bristlenose asks you to pick
once (\fBbristlenose use\fR) rather than guessing.
\fBazure\fR uses Azure OpenAI Service for
enterprise environments. \fBlocal\fR runs the analysis through Ollama on your
own hardware \(em no API key and no outbound call, but slower and it wants a
capable machine.
.TP
.BR \-\-codebook " " \fISLUG\fR
Apply a codebook framework during analysis. Run \fBbristlenose codebooks\fR to
list the available slugs.
.TP
.BR \-\-redact\-pii
Redact personally identifying information from transcripts. PII is retained by
default.
.TP
.BR \-\-retain\-pii
Retain PII in transcripts (default behaviour). Mutually exclusive with
\fB\-\-redact\-pii\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-skip\-transcription
Skip audio transcription (use existing transcripts).
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIPATH\fR
Path to a \fIbristlenose.toml\fR config file.
.TP
.BR \-\-clean
Delete the output directory before running.
.TP
.BR \-\-no\-serve
Suppress the auto-serve step at the end of the pipeline. By default, \fBrun\fR
serves the report on a free port and opens it in the browser. Hidden from
\fB\-\-help\fR; it exists for embedding contexts \(em notably the macOS app,
whose sidecar manages the serve port itself.
.TP
.BR \-\-dev
Development mode: enable the responsive playground in the served report
(grid overlay, breakpoint widget, design-system browser). Has no effect with
\fB\-\-no\-serve\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-no\-fetch
Abort instead of downloading missing runtime-fetched models (Whisper, spaCy)
or installing system binaries (ffmpeg via Homebrew). Run
\fBbristlenose doctor \-\-fetch\fR ahead of time to pre-warm the Whisper
cache for offline / air-gapped use.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Enable verbose logging.
.SS Options for \fBtranscribe\fR
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " " \fIDIR\fR
Output directory. Default: \fIbristlenose-output/\fR inside the input folder.
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-whisper\-model " " \fIMODEL\fR
Whisper model size.
.TP
.BR \-\-no\-fetch
Abort instead of downloading the Whisper model if it isn't cached.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Enable verbose logging.
.SS Options for \fBanalyze\fR
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " " \fIDIR\fR
Output directory. Default: parent of \fItranscripts-dir\fR if it's named
\fBtranscripts-raw\fR / \fBtranscripts-cooked\fR, otherwise creates
\fIbristlenose-output/\fR alongside.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-project " " \fINAME\fR
Project name.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-llm " " \fIPROVIDER\fR
LLM provider. Same values as for \fBrun\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-codebook " " \fISLUG\fR
Apply a codebook framework during analysis. Run \fBbristlenose codebooks\fR to
list the available slugs.
.TP
.BR \-\-no\-fetch
Abort instead of downloading missing runtime-fetched models. Used together
with \fBbristlenose doctor \-\-fetch\fR for offline runs.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Enable verbose logging.
.SS Options for \fBserve\fR
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-port " " \fIPORT\fR
Port to serve on. Default: \fB8150\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-palette " " \fINAME\fR
Colour palette for the report: \fBdefault\fR or \fBedo\fR.
Also set by \fBBRISTLENOSE_PALETTE\fR. Default: \fBdefault\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-dev
Development mode: auto-reload on Python changes, live JS reload, design
artifact browser.
.TP
.BR \-\-open " / " \-\-no\-open
Open the report in the default browser (default: \fB\-\-open\fR).
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Enable verbose logging.
.SS Options for \fBstatus\fR
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Show per-session detail with completion status.
.SS Options for \fBconfigure\fR
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-key " " \fIKEY\fR
API key to store. If not provided, prompts interactively.
.SS Options for \fBpipeline\fR
.TP
.BR \-\-json
Machine-readable JSON output, for scripting.
.TP
.BR \-\-stage " " \fIID\fR
Show one stage only, by id \(em for example \fBquote_extraction\fR.
.SS Options for \fBdoctor\fR
.TP
.BR \-\-fetch
Pre-download the Whisper transcription model (\(ti1.5 GB) so subsequent
\fBrun\fR / \fBtranscribe\fR invocations work offline or with
\fB\-\-no\-fetch\fR. Honours the \fI~/.cache/huggingface/hub/\fR cache root
(or \fBHF_HUB_CACHE\fR / \fBHF_HOME\fR if set). Idempotent and Ctrl+C-resumable.
.TP
.BR \-\-self\-test
Run bundle-integrity checks only (asserts every runtime-data file the
sidecar expects is present and non-trivial). Used by
\fBdesktop/scripts/build-all.sh\fR to fail-loud at build time when
PyInstaller \fBdatas\fR misses a runtime file. Exits non-zero on any
failure. Not for end-user use.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Settings are loaded in order (last wins):
.IP 1. 4
Built-in defaults
.IP 2. 4
\fI.env\fR file (searched upward from the current directory)
.IP 3. 4
Environment variables with prefix \fBBRISTLENOSE_\fR
.IP 4. 4
CLI flags
.PP
API keys have special priority: system credential store \(-> environment variable \(->
\fI.env\fR file. Use \fBbristlenose configure claude\fR, \fBbristlenose configure chatgpt\fR,
\fBbristlenose configure azure\fR, or \fBbristlenose configure gemini\fR to store keys
securely in the system credential store (macOS Keychain, Linux Secret Service).
.SS API keys
.TP
.B BRISTLENOSE_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
Claude API key.
.TP
.B BRISTLENOSE_OPENAI_API_KEY
ChatGPT API key.
.TP
.B BRISTLENOSE_GOOGLE_API_KEY
Gemini API key.
.SS Azure OpenAI settings
.TP
.B BRISTLENOSE_AZURE_API_KEY
Azure OpenAI API key (from the Azure portal).
.TP
.B BRISTLENOSE_AZURE_ENDPOINT
Azure OpenAI endpoint URL (e.g. \fBhttps://my-resource.openai.azure.com/\fR).
.TP
.B BRISTLENOSE_AZURE_DEPLOYMENT
Azure OpenAI deployment name (defined in the Azure portal, not a model name).
.TP
.B BRISTLENOSE_AZURE_API_VERSION
Azure OpenAI API version. Default: \fB2024-10-21\fR.
.SS LLM settings
.TP
.B BRISTLENOSE_LLM_PROVIDER
\fBanthropic\fR, \fBopenai\fR, \fBazure\fR, \fBgoogle\fR, or \fBlocal\fR.
Overrides the current provider set with \fBbristlenose use\fR /
\fBconfigure\fR; overridden in turn by \fB\-\-llm\fR.
.TP
.B BRISTLENOSE_LLM_MODEL
Model name. Defaults to the selected provider's recommended model.
.TP
.B BRISTLENOSE_LLM_MAX_TOKENS
Maximum response tokens. Default: \fB8192\fR.
.TP
.B BRISTLENOSE_LLM_TEMPERATURE
Sampling temperature. Default: \fB0.1\fR.
.TP
.B BRISTLENOSE_LLM_CONCURRENCY
Parallel LLM calls. Default: \fB3\fR.
.SS Local LLM settings (Ollama)
When no API key is configured and you run bristlenose, it prints setup
guidance \(em where to get a key for each cloud provider, and
\fBbristlenose configure local\fR for local models \(em and exits. If you
choose Local and Ollama isn't installed, bristlenose offers to install it
automatically (Homebrew on macOS, snap on Linux, curl script fallback). If
Ollama is installed but not running, bristlenose will start it for you.
.TP
.B BRISTLENOSE_LOCAL_URL
Ollama API endpoint. Default: \fBhttp://localhost:11434/v1\fR.
.TP
.B BRISTLENOSE_LOCAL_MODEL
Local model name. Default: \fBllama3.2:3b\fR. Other options: \fBllama3.1:8b\fR,
\fBmistral:7b\fR, \fBqwen2.5:7b\fR.
.SS Transcription settings
.TP
.B BRISTLENOSE_WHISPER_BACKEND
\fBauto\fR, \fBmlx\fR, or \fBfaster-whisper\fR. Default: \fBauto\fR.
.TP
.B BRISTLENOSE_WHISPER_MODEL
Model size. Default: \fBlarge-v3-turbo\fR.
.TP
.B BRISTLENOSE_WHISPER_LANGUAGE
Language code. Default: \fBen\fR.
.TP
.B BRISTLENOSE_WHISPER_DEVICE
Device for faster-whisper: \fBcpu\fR, \fBcuda\fR, or \fBauto\fR. Default: \fBauto\fR.
.TP
.B BRISTLENOSE_WHISPER_COMPUTE_TYPE
Compute type for faster-whisper: \fBint8\fR, \fBfloat16\fR, or \fBfloat32\fR. Default: \fBint8\fR.
.SS PII settings
.TP
.B BRISTLENOSE_PII_ENABLED
Enable PII redaction. Default: \fBfalse\fR.
.TP
.B BRISTLENOSE_PII_LLM_PASS
\fBNot implemented.\fR Reserved for a planned LLM-based second pass. Setting it
to true makes a redaction run stop with an error rather than silently redacting
with Presidio alone. Default: \fBfalse\fR.
.TP
.B BRISTLENOSE_PII_CUSTOM_NAMES
\fBNot implemented.\fR Reserved for a list of additional names to always redact.
Setting it makes a redaction run stop with an error, because the listed names
would not in fact be removed. Default: empty.
.SS Pipeline settings
.TP
.B BRISTLENOSE_MIN_QUOTE_WORDS
Minimum words per extracted quote. Default: \fB5\fR.
.TP
.B BRISTLENOSE_MERGE_SPEAKER_GAP_SECONDS
Gap threshold for merging consecutive speaker segments. Default: \fB2.0\fR.
.SS Preflight / runtime
.TP
.B BRISTLENOSE_SKIP_PREFLIGHT
When set to \fB1\fR, skip the first-run API-key preflight (paid \fI/messages\fR
validation call). Use on CI / scripted runs where the TTY heuristic isn't
reliable (Buildkite, \fIscript(1)\fR wrappers, tmux-from-cron).
.TP
.B BRISTLENOSE_LOG_LEVEL
Log file verbosity (\fI<output-dir>/.bristlenose/bristlenose.log\fR). Default:
\fBINFO\fR. The \fB\-v\fR flag controls terminal verbosity independently.
.TP
.B BRISTLENOSE_WHISPER_MODEL_DIR
Directory containing pre-downloaded Whisper models, used by the desktop
sidecar to bypass the runtime cache. Not needed for CLI use.
.TP
.B HF_HUB_CACHE \fR/ \fBHF_HOME
Hugging Face Hub cache locations \(em respected by the Whisper preflight when
determining whether the model is cached.
.SS Display settings
.TP
.B BRISTLENOSE_PALETTE
Colour palette for the report: \fBdefault\fR or \fBedo\fR. Also set by
\fBserve \-\-palette\fR. Default: \fBdefault\fR.
.TP
.B BRISTLENOSE_COLOR_SCHEME
Report theme: \fBauto\fR, \fBlight\fR, or \fBdark\fR. Default: \fBauto\fR.
.SH INPUT FILES
.B bristlenose
accepts any mix of audio, video, subtitle, and transcript files:
.PP
.RS
.nf
Audio:       .wav .mp3 .m4a .flac .ogg .wma .aac .aiff .aif .caf
Video:       .mp4 .m4v .mov .avi .mkv .webm .wmv .asf .mts .m2ts
             .3gp .flv .mpg .mpeg
Subtitles:   .srt .vtt
Transcripts: .docx (Microsoft Teams exports), .txt
.fi
.RE
.PP
Files sharing a name stem (e.g. \fIp1.mp4\fR and \fIp1.srt\fR) are treated as
a single session. When subtitles or transcripts exist, transcription is skipped
for that session.
.PP
Platform naming conventions are auto-detected for session grouping: Microsoft
Teams recording/transcript suffixes, Zoom cloud prefixes and meeting IDs, Zoom
local recording folders, and Google Meet parenthetical timestamps are all
stripped before stem comparison.
.SH OUTPUT
Output goes inside the input folder by default (avoids collisions when
processing multiple projects):
.PP
.RS
.nf
interviews/                          input folder
  bristlenose-output/                output folder (inside input)
    bristlenose-interviews-report.html    browsable report
    bristlenose-interviews-report.md      Markdown version
    people.yaml                           participant registry
    assets/
      bristlenose-theme.css               stylesheet
      bristlenose-logo.png                logo (light)
      bristlenose-logo-dark.png           logo (dark)
      bristlenose-player.html             popout video player
    sessions/
      transcript_s1.html                  per-session transcript pages
      transcript_s2.html
    transcripts-raw/                      one .txt and .md per session
    transcripts-cooked/                   PII-redacted (only with --redact-pii)
    .bristlenose/
      intermediate/                       JSON snapshots for re-rendering
      temp/                               FFmpeg scratch files
.fi
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
Full pipeline run (output created inside input folder):
.PP
.RS
.nf
bristlenose interviews
# Creates interviews/bristlenose-output/
.fi
.RE
.PP
Full pipeline with custom output location:
.PP
.RS
.nf
bristlenose run interviews -o results/ -p "Q1 Usability Study"
.fi
.RE
.PP
Transcribe only (no API key needed):
.PP
.RS
.nf
bristlenose transcribe interviews
.fi
.RE
.PP
Use Azure OpenAI (enterprise):
.PP
.RS
.nf
export BRISTLENOSE_AZURE_ENDPOINT=https://my-resource.openai.azure.com/
export BRISTLENOSE_AZURE_DEPLOYMENT=gpt-4o-research
bristlenose configure azure
bristlenose run interviews --llm azure
.fi
.RE
.PP
Use Gemini:
.PP
.RS
.nf
bristlenose configure gemini
bristlenose run interviews --llm gemini
.fi
.RE
.PP
Switch the current provider (keys stay stored):
.PP
.RS
.nf
bristlenose use chatgpt
.fi
.RE
.PP
Use local AI via Ollama (free, no API key):
.PP
.RS
.nf
bristlenose run interviews --llm local
# Requires Ollama running: ollama serve
.fi
.RE
.PP
Analyse existing transcripts:
.PP
.RS
.nf
bristlenose analyze interviews/bristlenose-output/transcripts-raw/
.fi
.RE
.PP
Re-open a previous report without re-running the pipeline:
.PP
.RS
.nf
bristlenose serve interviews
.fi
.RE
.PP
Check project status (read-only):
.PP
.RS
.nf
bristlenose status interviews
bristlenose status interviews -v    # per-session detail
.fi
.RE
.PP
Check dependencies and setup:
.PP
.RS
.nf
bristlenose doctor
.fi
.RE
.PP
Pre-warm the Whisper cache for an offline run:
.PP
.RS
.nf
bristlenose doctor \-\-fetch         # downloads \(ti1.5 GB once
bristlenose run interviews \-\-no\-fetch
# Now safe on a flight / air-gapped network
.fi
.RE
.PP
Skip the API-key preflight on a CI runner that has a known-good key:
.PP
.RS
.nf
BRISTLENOSE_SKIP_PREFLIGHT=1 bristlenose run interviews
.fi
.RE
.PP
Show configuration reference:
.PP
.RS
.nf
bristlenose help config
.fi
.RE
.SH HARDWARE
Transcription hardware is auto-detected:
.IP \(bu 4
Apple Silicon: MLX on Metal GPU
.IP \(bu 4
NVIDIA: faster-whisper with CUDA
.IP \(bu 4
Other: CPU fallback
.SH FILES
.TP
.I .env
Environment variables file, searched upward from the current directory.
.TP
.I .env.example
Template with all available configuration variables.
.TP
.I bristlenose.toml
Optional TOML configuration file.
.TP
.I ~/Library/Application Support/Bristlenose/state.json \fR(macOS)
.TQ
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/Bristlenose/state.json \fR(Linux, default
.IR ~/.local/share/Bristlenose/state.json )
Per-user preflight state \(em records the last successful API-key
validation timestamp per provider (24-hour TTL) so subsequent runs skip
the paid \fI/messages\fR call. Mode \fB0600\fR. Contains no API keys and
no transcript data. Delete the file to force re-validation on next run.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/huggingface/hub/ \fR(or \fB$HF_HUB_CACHE\fR)
Whisper model cache. Several GB depending on chosen model. Pre-warm with
\fBbristlenose doctor \-\-fetch\fR for offline / air-gapped use.
.TP
.I <output-dir>/.bristlenose/bristlenose.log
Per-project log file (default level \fBINFO\fR; override with
\fBBRISTLENOSE_LOG_LEVEL\fR).
.TP
.I <output-dir>/.bristlenose/pipeline-events.jsonl
Append-only forensic event log (run start / complete / cancel / fail with
structured failure cause). Read by the desktop diagnostic popover.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Error (missing input, configuration problem, pipeline failure).
.TP
.B 2
Preflight aborted: a required dependency is missing and could not be
auto-installed (e.g. ffmpeg not found and Homebrew unavailable / declined),
\fB\-\-no\-fetch\fR was set with an uncached Whisper model, or API-key
validation rejected the key (invalid, billing-empty, model-unavailable).
The terminal message names the recovery action.
